{
  "dom_id": "step-q2795",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14187947/assets/52448daf1f9aea06b4ab4713756080ddb3ab465b4fae8f92b65a54c251a81d5e.png)\n\nThe length of a rectangular prism is decreasing by $8\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}$ and its height increasing at a rate of $1\\,\\text{cm/min}.$ If the volume of the rectangular prism is decreasing at a rate of $50\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/min},$  how fast is its width changing when its dimensions are $10\\,\\text{cm}$ in length, $15\\,\\text{cm}$ in width and $5\\,\\text{cm}$ in height?",
  "worked_solution": "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the solid, and let $V$ be its volume. We are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =10\\text{ cm}, \\\\ y & =5\\text{ cm}, \\\\ z & =15\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-8\\text{ cm}\\text{/min}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =1\\text{ cm}\\text{/min}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =-50{\\text{ cm}}^{3}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}$ when $x=10\\,\\text{cm},$ $y=5\\,\\text{cm},$ and $z=15\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nWe start with the formula for the volume of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nV=xyz\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x\\cdot y\\cdot z) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =xy(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})+xz(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})+yz(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known values into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-50 & =(10)(5)(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})+(10)(15)(1)+(15)(5)(-8) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} & =8\\text{ cm}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the width of the solid is increasing at a rate of $8\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}$ at the moment when $x=10\\,\\text{cm},$ $y=5\\,\\text{cm},$ and $z=15\\,\\text{cm}.$",
